From e929323b24b535774a4918e9e1a9b6c4d5e1cbc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:29:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add a port to the Yoton YM03 (Actions ATJ2157)

New target yotonym03: Cortex-M4 at 48 MHz with 320 KiB of SRAM, SPI NOR,
SD card, 128x128 LCD, internal DAC, FOTG210 USB.

The firmware is demand-paged from NOR: a ~76 KiB resident image plus a
page store of 8 KiB code/rodata pages linked at SRAM2/SRAM3 aliases and
cached in 1 KiB lines through an MPU region pool (pager-atj2157.c,
tools in the yoton repository).

Drivers: system/timer/watchdog, pager, LCD, backlight, buttons (two
resistor ladders), SD host, PCM (DAC + DMA), USB device (mass storage).

Small-memory changes (MEMORYSIZE < 2): built-in minimp3 MP3/MP2/MP1
decoder on the FPU; plugins load into the codec area; windowed listing
of directories larger than the browser buffer, with playlists continuing
across windows; smaller buffers and stacks; buffering tuned for a few
KiB of file buffer; UI yield points so long UI work cannot starve the
decoder; USB mode frees the playback buffer.

Includes host test-mode hooks (apps/main.c, active only when the host
test tool arms them through RAM markers).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
